  "details": "VRChat Version:\nAvatar SDK 2022.08.29.20.48\nDescription of the bug:\nAvatar controls of the type submenu retain their value when a different type is selected, and are evaluated as if they were still a submenu during building.  This can prevent upload if a control previously pointed to a submenu that is no longer in use on the avatar that contains a control with a parameter no longer in use on the avatar\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n1. Create a submenu FOO and add it to an avatar's menu\n2. In that submenu FOO create a control that depends on some synced parameter BAR\n3. Remove parameter BAR\n4. Change the submenu FOO control on the avatar's menu to some other control, such as a radial puppet using parameter BAZ\n5. The builder will now report that parameter BAR is missing, and will point to submenu FOO as having the issue, despite FOO no longer being in use on the avatar \nNotes:\nDeleting the submenu control's reference to the menu, then changing the control type, allows for avatars to be uploaded",
